{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00411",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 0.72,
      "end_seconds": 4.95,
      "duration_seconds": 4.23,
      "text": "Doctor, if you're free, we can start. I've got the numbers noted down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 9.08,
      "end_seconds": 11.89,
      "duration_seconds": 2.81,
      "text": "Okay, thanks. Hi, how can I help today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 13.29,
      "end_seconds": 21.89,
      "duration_seconds": 8.6,
      "text": "So, I wanted to get palpitations looked at. A neighbour of mine said I should see someone about it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 22.45,
      "end_seconds": 26.92,
      "duration_seconds": 4.47,
      "text": "And when did that start? These questions might sound routine, but they matter."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 28.11,
      "end_seconds": 37.8,
      "duration_seconds": 9.69,
      "text": "About... well, three weeks. I'd rather not end up on lots of tablets if I can avoid it. Sorry, I know I'm rambling a bit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 39.06,
      "end_seconds": 41.99,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "How would you describe it, mild, moderate, severe?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 43.43,
      "end_seconds": 46.08,
      "duration_seconds": 2.65,
      "text": "A five out of ten, I suppose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 46.44,
      "end_seconds": 50.03,
      "duration_seconds": 3.59,
      "text": "Alright. Sorry about the noise outside, the building work never stops."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 51.13,
      "end_seconds": 53.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.6,
      "text": "I, I hadn't even noticed, honestly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 54.59,
      "end_seconds": 56.77,
      "duration_seconds": 2.18,
      "text": "Any fainting or leg swelling at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 57.94,
      "end_seconds": 60.31,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "No, none of that at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 64.25,
      "end_seconds": 75.57,
      "duration_seconds": 11.32,
      "text": "I like to make sure you understand what's happening, so please stop me at any point. There are no silly questions, and I'd much rather you ask now than go home still wondering about something."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 76.17,
      "end_seconds": 77.87,
      "duration_seconds": 1.7,
      "text": "Right, I understand now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 78.55,
      "end_seconds": 79.5,
      "duration_seconds": 0.95,
      "text": "Any regular medication?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 83.16,
      "end_seconds": 84.57,
      "duration_seconds": 1.41,
      "text": "No, nothing regular."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 85.38,
      "end_seconds": 88.81,
      "duration_seconds": 3.43,
      "text": "Do you have any questions before we carry on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 91.85,
      "end_seconds": 103.62,
      "duration_seconds": 11.77,
      "text": "Not at the moment, uh, I think you've covered most of what I was wondering. If something comes to mind later, I'll ask you before I leave."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 104.64,
      "end_seconds": 108.5,
      "duration_seconds": 3.86,
      "text": "What about allergies, to medicines or foods or anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 109.3,
      "end_seconds": 113.6,
      "duration_seconds": 4.3,
      "text": "So, I'm allergic to ibuprofen, I get stomach pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 114.86,
      "end_seconds": 132.16,
      "duration_seconds": 17.3,
      "text": "What I'm doing here is putting together three things: what you tell me, what I find when I examine you, and what the tests show. None of those alone is enough, which is why we sometimes need to wait for results before being certain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 132.53,
      "end_seconds": 135.64,
      "duration_seconds": 3.11,
      "text": "Okay, so I appreciate you explaining that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 136.49,
      "end_seconds": 139.64,
      "duration_seconds": 3.15,
      "text": "Any medical conditions, anything you've been treated for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 141.08,
      "end_seconds": 143.9,
      "duration_seconds": 2.82,
      "text": "No, I've never had anything serious."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 145.24,
      "end_seconds": 148.23,
      "duration_seconds": 2.99,
      "text": "Sorry, the computer needs a moment to load this."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 148.96,
      "end_seconds": 149.76,
      "duration_seconds": 0.8,
      "text": "No rush."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 159.86,
      "end_seconds": 162.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.29,
      "text": "Okay, here we go. Do you smoke?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 163.19,
      "end_seconds": 165.7,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "I smoke about ten cigarettes a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 166.38,
      "end_seconds": 167.78,
      "duration_seconds": 1.4,
      "text": "So, what about alcohol?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 168.99,
      "end_seconds": 172.56,
      "duration_seconds": 3.57,
      "text": "A beer or two most evenings, to be honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 173.06,
      "end_seconds": 181.39,
      "duration_seconds": 8.33,
      "text": "Here are the numbers, doctor. Heart rate 114, temperature is 36.5 degrees. Respiratory rate 16, SpO2 99 percent on room air, pressure 134 over 77."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 182.3,
      "end_seconds": 183.43,
      "duration_seconds": 1.13,
      "text": "Good, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 184.14,
      "end_seconds": 186.8,
      "duration_seconds": 2.66,
      "text": "Let me double-check something in your record."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 187.22,
      "end_seconds": 189.16,
      "duration_seconds": 1.94,
      "text": "Of course, take your time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 202.55,
      "end_seconds": 204.23,
      "duration_seconds": 1.68,
      "text": "Okay, here we go."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 205.29,
      "end_seconds": 209.33,
      "duration_seconds": 4.04,
      "text": "Alright, I'd like to examine you now. Please come over here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 211.16,
      "end_seconds": 213.53,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "Now bend it for me, slowly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 224.64,
      "end_seconds": 227.19,
      "duration_seconds": 2.55,
      "text": "No murmurs and the neck veins aren't distended."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 228.49,
      "end_seconds": 230.95,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "Okay, just relax, I'll be quick."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 244.56,
      "end_seconds": 246.51,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "Pulse is irregular right now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 251.46,
      "end_seconds": 257.53,
      "duration_seconds": 6.07,
      "text": "Okay, you can sit back up. I'll try to keep this as efficient as I can."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 258.61,
      "end_seconds": 260.74,
      "duration_seconds": 2.13,
      "text": "Thank you, I appreciate it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 261.33,
      "end_seconds": 279.13,
      "duration_seconds": 17.8,
      "text": "So, based on the history and the examination, my working impression is a possible heart rhythm problem like atrial fibrillation. I want to be honest that this is an impression, not a final answer. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had palpitations for three weeks, and no leg swelling or fainting."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 279.73,
      "end_seconds": 282.89,
      "duration_seconds": 3.16,
      "text": "Exactly, um, that's what's been happening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 283.72,
      "end_seconds": 287.92,
      "duration_seconds": 4.2,
      "text": "Give me a second, I'm just scrolling back through your chart."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 288.32,
      "end_seconds": 289.12,
      "duration_seconds": 0.8,
      "text": "Of course."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 304.61,
      "end_seconds": 324.26,
      "duration_seconds": 19.65,
      "text": "Alright, I've got it. We should do a thyroid test for palpitations. That will help us see what's going on underneath and decide the next step. I'm prescribing metoprolol, 25 milligrams, twice a day, until we review. You take it by mouth. That's for palpitations. Cut back on tea, coffee and energy drinks, and note the time whenever it happens."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 325.45,
      "end_seconds": 342.72,
      "duration_seconds": 17.27,
      "text": "Try to get to bed and wake up at the same time each day, and keep your phone away from the bed. Keep an eye out, and if you faint or have chest pain with the racing, call us the same day or go to emergency."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 343.51,
      "end_seconds": 345.29,
      "duration_seconds": 1.78,
      "text": "Got it, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 345.77,
      "end_seconds": 348.59,
      "duration_seconds": 2.82,
      "text": "Let's review you after the results are back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 352.1,
      "end_seconds": 354.13,
      "duration_seconds": 2.03,
      "text": "Right, okay, I'll book that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 354.48,
      "end_seconds": 359.35,
      "duration_seconds": 4.87,
      "text": "Let me check that I've been clear. What will you do once you get home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 360.05,
      "end_seconds": 369.0,
      "duration_seconds": 8.95,
      "text": "So, I take the metoprolol, 25 milligrams, twice a day and come back after the results are back. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 369.58,
      "end_seconds": 373.23,
      "duration_seconds": 3.65,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Okay, we're done for today. Take care."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 374.0,
      "end_seconds": 376.5,
      "duration_seconds": 2.5,
      "text": "Nothing more from me, doctor, thanks."
    }
  ]
}